## 10. Output requirements

1. Write a comprehensive, technically detailed referee report suitable for a research journal in mathematics.
2. Use precise mathematical language and appropriate LaTeX notation.
3. Identify exact page numbers, theorem numbers, equations, and proof locations whenever possible.
4. Provide verifiable bibliographic references and hyperlinks.
5. Clearly distinguish verified findings from unconfirmed suspicions.
6. Do not include generic praise, positive assessments, or descriptions of correct mathematics.
7. Give particular prominence to substantial missing references and disguised previously known arguments.
8. Explicitly identify confirmed instances of AI slop and supply standard terminology.
9. Treat insufficient mathematical significance as a major concern when supported by the research comparison.
10. Include this entire instruction prompt verbatim, exactly once, in an appendix titled **"Referee Instructions"**, without recursive duplication.
11. Set the author of the referee report to **ChatGPT-6**.
12. Export the report as a complete, standalone, compilable **LaTeX (.tex) file**.
13. Also produce a compiled PDF whenever technically possible.
14. Ensure that the bibliography, mathematics, hyperlinks, and document structure compile correctly.
15. Complete as much of the investigation as the available tools and sources permit. Explicitly disclose limitations instead of claiming exhaustive verification without evidence.

